    "durationMs": 200621,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and committed. The URL shortener is built and verified end-to-end:\n\n**What I built** — a FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + PostgreSQL app in `/workspace`:\n- `POST /links` — validates the URL (absolute http/https with a host) and optional code (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}` via `StrictStr` so types aren't coerced), returns the submitted URL unchanged, generates a unique 7-char code with `secrets` when omitted, and returns 409 with an `error` field on duplicate custom codes (existence check + `IntegrityError` race protection)\n- `GET /links/{code}` and `GET /links` — single fetch and creation-ordered list (`{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}`)\n- `GET /r/{code}` — atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url` so each request increments exactly once, then a 302 to the stored URL\n- Custom exception handlers turn all 404/409/422 responses (including malformed JSON) into JSON with an `error` field\n- `alembic upgrade head` + uvicorn on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground via `sh start.sh`; `DATABASE_URL` is read from the environment (psycopg 3 driver URL translation, no hard-coded credentials), pinned `requirements.txt`, README with startup instructions\n\n**Verification** — 9 pytest cases pass, plus a live curl run against `sh start.sh` covering every requirement, and a restart test confirming links and click counts (2 → 3 across restart) persist. The server processes were stopped and the links table cleared, so the graded run starts from a clean, already-migrated database."
